            <div xml:id="preface">

                <pb facs="0007" n="III" xml:id="pgIII"/>

                <head>Preface</head>
                <p>This volume was prepared in the Historical Office under the direct supervision of
                    the late S. Everett Gleason and of Fredrick Aandahl, who succeeded him as Editor
                    of <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi> in 1972.</p>
                <p>William Z. Slany prepared all sections of the volume except those on relations
                    with the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics, which were prepared by Rogers P.
                    Churchill.</p>
                <p>The editors acknowledge with appreciation the assistance provided them by the
                    historians of the Department of Defense, including the Joint Chiefs of Staff.
                    They are also grateful for the cooperation of the National Security Council, the
                    Department of Defense, the Department of Commerce, and the Central Intelligence
                    Agency, all of which concurred in the declassification of various papers for
                    release herein.</p>
                <p>The technical editing of this volume was done by Helen V. Gilbert of the
                    Publishing and Reproduction Division, headed by Willard M. McLaughlin. The index
                    was prepared by Francis C. Prescott.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fredrick Aandahl</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Director, Historical Office</hi>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Bureau of Public Affairs</hi>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="preface-a1.xml" xpointer="preface-a1"/>
